@startuml seq_sft_upshifts
title SC-SFT-03 - Upshifts 1 -> 4 while accelerating

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SFT-001, SYS-SFT-003, SYS-SFT-004, SYS-SFT-007, SYS-ACT-001, SYS-ACT-002, SYS-SEN-005,
SIM-PLT-003, SIM-PLT-006
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
Ratios 1st 3.06, 2nd 1.63, 3rd 1.00, 4th 0.70 (system_context section 4.1).
end note

note over TCU: D in 1st, mode Normal
User -> Console : throttle
Console -> Plant : Throttle
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> Plant : vehicle accelerates (SIM-PLT-006)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Throttle; SIM_Speed: InputShaftSpeed, OutputShaftSpeed
end

== shift 1 -> 2 ==
TCU -> TCU : upshift table (vehicle speed, throttle) gives target gear 2 (SYS-SFT-001)
TCU -> TCU : t1: start shift 1 -> 2, one step (SYS-SFT-003); shift in progress
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = ON (2nd, SYS-ACT-001),\nPCS_Duty from the shift pressure profile (SYS-ACT-002)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: GearTarget = 2, ShiftInProgress = 1
Plant -> Plant : engages 2nd: InputShaftSpeed moves from ratio 3.06 to 1.63 over 400 ms (SIM-PLT-003)
note over TCU: no ratio plausibility check while a shift is in progress (SYS-SEN-005)
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: InputShaftSpeed, OutputShaftSpeed
end
... InputShaftSpeed / OutputShaftSpeed within +/- 5 % of 1.63 for 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t2: shift complete (SYS-SFT-007)
note right of TCU: t2 - t1 < 800 ms, otherwise shift fault (SC-SFT-06)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = ON, PCS_Duty from the table\n(throttle, gear) (SYS-ACT-002)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: GearActual = 2, ShiftInProgress = 0

== shift 2 -> 3 ==
opt the schedule asks for 3rd earlier than 2000 ms after t2
  TCU -> TCU : shift not started yet (SYS-SFT-004)
end
... >= 2000 ms after t2 (SYS-SFT-004) ...
TCU -> TCU : target gear 3: start shift 2 -> 3
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF (3rd), shift pressure profile
Plant -> Plant : ratio 1.63 -> 1.00 over 400 ms
... ratio within +/- 5 % of 1.00 for 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t3: shift complete
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: PCS_Duty from the table

== shift 3 -> 4 ==
... >= 2000 ms after t3 (SYS-SFT-004) ...
TCU -> TCU : target gear 4: start shift 3 -> 4
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = ON, SS_B = OFF (4th), shift pressure profile
Plant -> Plant : ratio 1.00 -> 0.70 over 400 ms
... ratio within +/- 5 % of 0.70 for 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t4: shift complete
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: PCS_Duty from the table; TCU_Status: GearActual = 4

note over Plant, TCU: Limp-home outputs are not delayed by SYS-SFT-004 (SYS-SFT-004 note, SYS-FLT-001 note).
@enduml
